What a blast of fresh air in our so threatened game world! Buy it, just buy it.
- Wonderful art;
- One of the best OSTs I've ever heard in a game;
- No DLCs;
- Great gameplay, surely on par with genre classics, like Contra, Alex Kidd and Altered Beast;
- No huge lights telling you what to do or where to go;
- No ~microtransactions~ a.k.a pay-to-win;
- No greedy cosmetic items, loot boxes et caterva. It means = no gambling. Ironic, lol
- Fair price.
Thank you Studio MDHR for bringing us this gem! Please don't take so long for Cuphead 2!

Good survival game if you're looking for some serious challenge and a realistic feel.  Everything is pretty well thought out.  There are a lot of customization options (including a Hard Survival mode, where enemies are much smarter & more aggressive and natural resources more sparse).  They frequently add content.  The story's worth it.  How you build and act will drastically affect how each local tribe views and interacts with you.
Only thing I can say against it is there are a couple of small bugs that have been a little hard for them to  fix so far;
Very, very rarely when you kill something or chop down a tree, you'll get tossed like 10-30 feet into the air and take a little fall damage is the only one that's seriously annoying/game affecting.  (Might happen once every 10-20 hours played).

